WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.234
-Guys, as I mentioned,
it is Nana Week

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.601
here at the show,
and we've been giving some love

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.901
to all the grandmas out there,
all the gammies,

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:12.467
all the meemaws,
the bubbies, yeah, the abuelas.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:13.934
Every night this week,
we've been shining

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.234
a spotlight on
a talented grandma.

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:18.133
Tonight's talented nana is
Debbie Bazza.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:22.300
She is from the Bronx, and --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.200
And she's gonna do some
stand-up comedy for us tonight.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.100
So without further ado,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.300
give a warm welcome to
Debbie Bazza!

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:40.901
-Hi, everybody.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.501
I'm so happy to be here
with all of you.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:48.167
I'm married 30 years.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.133
It took three husbands,

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.267
but it's still 30 years.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.434
Wow! What a
great-looking audience.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:58.901
Do I look okay?

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.701
Thank you. It's a lot of work.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.133
Between the creams,
moisturizers, and lotions,

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.133
I got into bed last night,
slid right on the floor.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.901
My two grown daughters
moved back home.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.734
That crap shouldn't be allowed.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:17.968
They were always fighting
and screaming growing up.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.501
One morning,
they're beating each other up

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.901
over the last pair of
school socks.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.968
I'm trying to open my eyes
and drink my coffee.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.067
I walked out of the room.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.467
I figure,
let the stronger one live.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.734
I don't care.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.100
And they would threaten me.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.634
"I'm running away.
I'm gonna run away."

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.467
So, I would reassure them
and tell them,

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.067
"Honey, you don't have
to run away.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:41.100
I'll get the car and take you
wherever you want to go."

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.367
Do me a favor --
take your sister with you.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.400
I like my own room.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.534
Your father's snoring
is keeping me up all night."

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:55.367
Isn't that the worst,
trying to sleep with a snorer?

00:01:55.367 --> 00:01:58.334
You've got that little window in
between "kuhhh!" and "kehhh!"

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.267
to fall asleep.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.534
He tried.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:07.167
He got the no-snore tape and
the no-snore spray.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.667
He even got a no-snore pillow.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:11.767
It kind of works if you put it
on his face and...

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:19.567
I just want to say
I love my daughters

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.868
and I'd do anything for them.

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.133
Maybe I'd do
a little more for one,

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.701
but, basically,
I'd do anything for them.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:28.567
You've been a great audience.
Thank you!

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.934
-Oh, my God!

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:35.000
You were phenomenal.
Thank you so much!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.300
Come on! Debbie Bazza!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.033
-Jimmy!
-Debbie Bazza!

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.734
-Oh, my God! Jimmy Fallon!
-That was Fantastic!

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:41.901
Oh, my God!

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.400
-Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.000
-And thank you
for signing my book.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.334
-Oh, my God.
-Oh, oh.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.033
-I'll sign your book.
Whatever you want, I'll do it.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.267
-Yes, that -- Oh, my God.
-Are you kidding me?

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:50.701
That snoring bit was fantastic.
I loved it.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:51.834
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.634
-Give it up for Debbie Bazza,
everybody.

